For the explicit two-port completion studied, r=2 has a stable weak-coupling c=1 region. In the family q₊=1, q₋=m, the leading SU(m) interaction becomes marginally relevant at m=7, r=14. A common filling shift does not remove this instability.

Distinct fillings with exact U(1)ᵐ symmetry provide a conditional repair. Their microscopic implementation remains necessary.

The supplied port compressions do not determine the joint excited-state resolvent, so the result does not establish stability for every mirror realization. The full second-order SW calculation, including adjacent bonds, passed two- and three-cell spectral checks with O(λ³) errors.

